  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 16-layer dielectric stack on Ge substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: ZnSe/ZnS alternating, starting with ZnSe (16 layers total). Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness centered at 9500 nm (ZnSe: ~620 nm, ZnS: ~750 nm assuming n_ZnSe≈2.4, n_ZnS≈2.2). Thickness bounds: 200-3000 nm per layer. Optimize for maximum mean transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band and minimum mean transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with multi-start from quarter-wave baseline. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 8000-11000 nm, 3000-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band; Low transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count not exceeding 16.",
